{
  "$comment": [
    "Every Google Search Central page a universal rule in this tool rests on, with the",
    "'Last updated' date printed on that page and the date we read it.",
    "",
    "This file is what makes 'follows current Google practice' a fact rather than a claim.",
    "`node scripts/google-sources.mjs` re-reads each page, compares the date, and fails",
    "when Google has moved — so drift becomes a build failure instead of a slow lie.",
    "tools/test.mjs asserts every id under `backs` exists in the rule catalogue, so a",
    "renamed check cannot orphan its source.",
    "",
    "A rule with no source here is HOUSE STYLE and says so in lib/policy.mjs. The point",
    "of the list is not to cover every rule; it is that anything called universal can",
    "be traced to a published page and a date."
  ],
